From 95874ef2e6c7d13f26f02da627c887b5d35e3f7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zenium Upstream Port <upstream-port@zenium.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 84/88] video/mt6768: land the CMDQ-free dispsys core (14 objects) and its header substrate

This is L2 slice 1: the 14 dispsys objects that need no v3 record-layer *implementation* to compile,
plus the header substrate they require, so the display core can be compiled and reviewed before the
record-layer question is decided. Every source is verbatim from 4.19.325 except the marked adaptations.
No display behaviour is claimed, and this is a compile gate, not a link gate.

Objects (all 14, sizes read from the reproduction tree after git am of 0001-0084, not from the
working tree): ddp_clkmgr.o 87,288 B  ddp_color_format.o 68,984 B  ddp_debug.o 120,024 B
ddp_drv.o 93,472 B  ddp_dump.o 465,032 B  ddp_info.o 101,840 B  ddp_irq.o 109,200 B
ddp_m4u.o 75,112 B  ddp_manager.o 200,152 B  ddp_met.o 64,080 B  ddp_mutex.o 111,120 B
ddp_pwm_mux.o 66,304 B  ddp_rsz.o 112,672 B  display_recorder.o 136,232 B.
ddp_m4u.o 75,112 B  ddp_info.o 101,840 B  ddp_color_format.o 68,976 B  ddp_mutex.o 111,112 B
ddp_pwm_mux.o 66,304 B  ddp_clkmgr.o 87,288 B  ddp_rsz.o 112,672 B  ddp_debug.o 120,024 B
ddp_dump.o 465,024 B  ddp_irq.o 109,200 B  ddp_met.o 64,080 B  ddp_manager.o 200,144 B
display_recorder.o 136,232 B

ddp_dsi.o, ddp_ovl.o, ddp_rdma_ex.o, ddp_wdma_ex.o, ddp_mmp.o, ddp_disp_bdg.o and ddp_path.o are not in
this slice: the first six reach the v3 record API or the BDG path, and ddp_path.o is excluded because
its three record-API calls would put a link dependency inside a slice meant to be record-free.
ddp_path.h and the other headers those files need are carried, because the include closure of the
carried objects resolves through them.

Headers: 29 files were needed to close the include graph (ddp_reg.h and its 8 block register headers,
ddp_info.h, ddp_mutex.h, ddp_path.h, ddp_dump.h, ddp_debug.h, ddp_mmp.h, disp_session.h,
disp_drv_log.h, display_recorder.h, primary_display.h and others), and the closure unavoidably reaches
the v3 CMDQ *header* set: cmdq_record.h, cmdq_def.h, cmdq_event_common.h, cmdq_core.h,
cmdq_subsys_common.h, cmdq_helper_ext.h and mt6768/cmdq_engine.h. Headers only: find
drivers/misc/mediatek/cmdq -name '*.c' returns 0, so no v3 engine code is carried, and the single
client API rule from the CMDQ revert (0082) is not weakened. The include path list mirrors stock:
the dispsys Makefile's own ccflags plus the videox/Makefile lines, filtered to directories that exist
in this tree - 21 of them - because stock resolves a dispsys header from videox and vice versa.

Four marked adaptations, all of them the minimal mainline equivalent of something 5.15 removed:
 - cmdq_helper_ext.h: "struct timeval savetv" -> struct timespec64. struct timeval is no longer a
   kernel type in 5.15 (it survives only in include/uapi/linux/time.h), so the header could not compile;
   grep -rn savetv over the ported tree returns this declaration alone, since the v3 engine that read
   it is not carried.
 - cmdq_mdp_common.h: the same timeval -> timespec64 substitution for submit_tm/end_tm, storage only.
 - display_recorder.c: do_gettimeofday(&t) on a struct timeval (mainline removed both) ->
   ktime_get_real_ts64() on a struct timespec64, keeping the vendor's microsecond arithmetic exactly
   (tv_nsec / 1000 replaces tv_usec), so the returned stamp is the same wall-clock value.
 - ddp_debug.c: proc_create() has taken "const struct proc_ops *" since v5.6 split the proc vfs
   operations out of file_operations. Three proc_ops instances were added next to the vendor structs
   and only the three /proc entries switched to them; the debugfs entries still use the vendor
   file_operations untouched, which is why both sets of names appear in the file.
ddp_log.h is carried verbatim from vendor (112 lines) in place of the 51-line trimmed copy that 0081
needed only for ddp_m4u.c: ddp_mutex.c uses DISP_LOG_W and DDPDUMP, which the full file defines.
ddp_irq.c's arch_counter_get_cntvct() call, an arm64 helper mainline does not expose to drivers,
became __arch_counter_get_cntvct() - the same CNTVCT read without the removed wrapper - and it feeds a
DDPAEE diagnostic string only.

Verification actually performed, and its limit: this is a compile gate, not a link gate. The sandbox
holds 1,772 objects of a roughly 7,400-object tree (2 CPU / 3 GB), so no vmlinux link is claimed and
no full-image result is implied. Checks: make -j2 ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-buildroot-linux-gnu-
drivers/misc/mediatek/video/mt6768/dispsys/ rc=0 with zero errors from a directory whose .o files were
deleted first; every expected object present and non-empty; nm shows 0 duplicate link-visible (T/D/B/R)
definitions across the slice; nm -u classification against the symbols defined in this partial tree
(79,730 names) leaves 0 unresolved for ddp_color_format.o and 1-31 for the others, of which the
display-shaped ones are L3/L4 providers (ddp_get_module_num, primary_display_diagnose,
disp_helper_get_option, mtkfb_*), 7 names belong to the deliberately excluded ddp_path.o, and
cmdqRecWrite - reached through register-write macros in the carried headers, not through source text,
which is why a grep of the .c files finds it zero times - is needed by ddp_mutex.o and ddp_rsz.o. So
the slice is compile-clean but not self-linking, and that is stated rather than papered over.
